{"author":{"id":"973fc03426eba9a243913e0f6e6823e102397744f60a9ab11c882af948c310c4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1774460299,"nonce":"xT6N7k6iffV+Xa11Hc0UO7UHOUM=","title":"Convention: all issue comments and results must reference source commit and script","message":"Every git-bug comment presenting experimental results or analysis output must include provenance metadata for reproducibility:\n\n1. **Script path** — the script that generated the results (e.g., `scripts/eval_null_space.py`)\n2. **Commit hash or branch** — the exact code version used (e.g., `feature/part2.5-analysis` at `abc1234`)\n3. **Model/data paths** — paths to trained models, datasets, or checkpoints consumed or produced\n\nThe same provenance standard applies to results directories: each output directory should contain (or its creation should be logged with) the script, commit, and input paths that produced it.\n\nThis is critical for reproducibility. Without provenance, results comments become orphaned data points that cannot be verified, reproduced, or extended by future sessions.","files":null}]}